input with its monitor gone: abandon the swipe, drop the touch motion

CUnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture keeps the monitor the swipe began on as a
weak reference (m_monitor), and update() and end() dereference it
unconditionally after checking only isGestureInProgress(), i.e. that
m_workspaceBegin is set.

If the monitor is removed mid-gesture, the reference expires and the
next event crashes. Reproduced on a laptop whose lid-close handler
disables the panel (eDP-1) via a monitor rule: a touchscreen swipe was
in progress as the lid closed, the panel was disabled and later
re-enabled as a new monitor, and the pending touch-up on lid-open
ran end() into a null m_monitor. Debug symbols for the crashed build put
the fault at end()'s `m_monitor->m_size.x` (SIGSEGV, via
CInputManager::onTouchUp). update() has the same unguarded dereference
and is the likely cause of earlier crashes in onTouchMove.

Both now abandon the swipe when the monitor is gone, the same way
update() already invalidates a swipe elsewhere: reset the starting
workspace's render offset and clear the gesture state.

Touch motion, the same failure on another path: onTouchMove's three
delivery branches (session-lock surface, window, layer surface) each
dereferenced their monitor unchecked. A finger moving while eDP-1 came
back after a lid close reached the window branch with an expired
m_monitor -- SIGSEGV in CInputManager::onTouchMove (2026-10-08 11:44,
crash report log tail: eDP-1 disabled, then re-enabled). The motion is
now dropped when that monitor is gone.

--- a/src/managers/input/UnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture.cpp	2026-09-28 13:37:35.893324432 +0900
+++ b/src/managers/input/UnifiedWorkspaceSwipeGesture.cpp	2026-09-28 13:37:35.949323217 +0900
@@ -41,6 +41,18 @@
     if (!isGestureInProgress())
         return;
 
+    // The monitor this swipe began on can disappear mid-gesture -- disabled by
+    // a monitor rule (a lid-close handler turning the panel off), unplugged --
+    // and m_monitor is only a weak reference, so everything below would
+    // dereference null. Abandon the swipe the way update() already does for an
+    // invalid one, putting the starting workspace back where it was.
+    if UNLIKELY (!m_monitor) {
+        m_workspaceBegin->m_renderOffset->setValueAndWarp(Vector2D(0, 0));
+        m_workspaceBegin   = nullptr;
+        m_initialDirection = 0;
+        return;
+    }
+
